"appellate-division-administrative-order-no-2601-use-generative-artificial-intelligence (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/local-rules/appellate-division-administrative-order-no-2601-use-generative-artificial-intelligence.pdf)\nciteturn1031view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn1027view1\",\"lineno\":0}); Total lines: 33\nL0@P0: \nL1@P0:  Superior Court of California\nL2@P0:  County of Orange\nL3@P0: Chambers of\nL4@P0: 700 CIVIC CENTER DRIVE WEST\nL5@P0: KIMBERLY A. KNILL SANTA ANA, CA 92701\nL6@P0: APPELLATE DIVISIOIN\nL7@P0: PRESIDING JUDGE PHONE: (657) 622-5231\nL8@P0: APPELLATE DIVISION ADMINISTRATIVE ORDER NO. 26/01\nL9@P0: USE OF GENERATIVE ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE\nL10@P0: Generative artificial intelligence (AI) tools that supply natural language answers to\nL11@P0: user prompts, such as ChatGPT, Harvey, CoCounsel, Claude, Grok, and Google Gemini,\nL12@P0: are now in wide use.\nL13@P0: Counsel and self-represented parties are responsible for providing the court with\nL14@P0: complete and accurate representations of the record, procedural history, and cited legal\nL15@P0: authorities. Use of generative AI is not prohibited, but counsel or the self-represented\nL16@P0: party must personally confirm for themselves the accuracy of any research conducted\nL17@P0: by these means, and counsel or the self-represented party alone bears ethical\nL18@P0: responsibility for all statements made in filings. The signature or listing of counsel or a\nL19@P0: self-represented party on a filing containing AI-generated content, including citations\nL20@P0: generated by AI, constitutes a certification the signer (and any attorney or other self\u0002represented party listed on the filing) has personally verified the content’s accuracy. The\nL21@P0: court will impute any errors by such AI tools to the signer and any other attorney or self\u0002represented party listed on the filing.\nL22@P0: Counsel for a party, or a self-represented party, choosing to use generative AI or\nL23@P0: other automated tools shall fully comply with any applicable protective order and all\nL24@P0: applicable ethical/legal obligations in their use, disclosure to, submission to, or other\nL25@P0: interaction with any such AI tools.\nL26@P0: Failure to verify the accuracy of submissions, particularly the accuracy of citations\nL27@P0: to law and evidence, may be grounds for sanctions or disciplinary action before the\nL28@P0: State Bar.\nL29@P0: IT IS SO ORDERED this 6th day of August, 2026, in Orange County, California.\nL30@P0: ___________________________\nL31@P0: Kimberly A. Knill\nL32@P0: Appellate Division Presiding Judge\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nc8a03ca0-1deb-4126-9614-dac654bd6350 (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/division_10.pdf)\nciteturn1031view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn1027view2\",\"lineno\":0}); Total lines: 29\nL0@P0: LOCAL RULES – SUPERIOR COURT of CALIFORNIA, COUNTY of ORANGE\nL1@P0: (issued 01/01/21)\nL2@P0: 10-1\nL3@P0: DIVISION 10\nL4@P0: LOCAL EMERGENCY RULE 1\nL5@P0: CASE MANAGEMENT\nL6@P0: CONFERENCES\nL7@P0: Rule Effective\nL8@P0-1: 1. Suspension of Case Management Conferences Due to Pandemic 01/01/21LOCAL RULES – SUPERIOR COURT of CALIFORNIA, COUNTY of ORANGE\nL9@P1: (issued 01/01/21)\nL10@P1: 10-2\nL11@P1: Division 10\nL12@P1: Local Emergency Rule 1\nL13@P1: Rule 1. Suspension of Case Management Conferences Due to Pandemic\nL14@P1: In response to the COVID-19 emergency’s devastating impacts on the court’s ability\nL15@P1: to conduct normal operations, the court is suspending case management conference\nL16@P1: procedures through March 31, 2021.\nL17@P1: Pursuant to California Rules of Court, rule 3.720(b), all limited and unlimited civil\nL18@P1: cases are exempted from the case management rules set forth in California Rules of Court, rules\nL19@P1: 3.721 to 3.730. This rule does not affect or apply to cases otherwise exempt from case\nL20@P1: management review. (See Cal. Rules of Court, rule 3.721.) This rule suspends the case\nL21@P1: management conference provisions of Local Rules 321, 355, 369, and 371 through March 31,\nL22@P1: 2021.\nL23@P1: All currently scheduled Case Management Conference (CMC) hearings are vacated. In\nL24@P1: addition, new cases filed through March 31, 2021, not already exempt from case management\nL25@P1: review, will not be set for a CMC hearing. For cases that otherwise would have been subject to\nL26@P1: the case management procedures, a Mandatory Settlement Conference (MSC) and Trial date\nL27@P1: will be scheduled by the court 19 to 21 months from the date the case was filed.\nL28@P1: Revised January 1, 2021; Approved effective May 6, 2020.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nl690 (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/l690.pdf)\nciteturn1031view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1005view3\",\"id\":316}); Total lines: 82\nL0@P0: ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY: STATE BAR NO.: FOR COURT USE ONLY\nL1@P0: For your protection and\nL2@P0: privacy, please press the\nL3@P0: Clear This Form button\nL4@P0: after you are done printing\nL5@P0: this form.\nL6@P0: NAME:\nL7@P0: FIRM NAME:\nL8@P0: STREET ADDRESS:\nL9@P0: CITY: STATE: ZIP CODE:\nL10@P0: TELEPHONE NO.:\nL11@P0: E-MAIL ADDRESS:\nL12@P0: ATTORNEY FOR (name):\nL13@P0: SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF ORANGE\nL14@P0: JUSTICE CENTER:\nL15@P0:  Central - 700 Civic Center Dr. West, Santa Ana, CA 92701-4045\nL16@P0:  Harbor-Newport Beach Facility - 4601 Jamboree Rd., Newport Beach, CA92660-2595\nL17@P0:  North - 1275 N. Berkeley Ave., P. O. Box 5000, Fullerton, CA 92838-0500\nL18@P0:  West – 8141 13th Street, Westminster, CA 92683-4593\nL19@P0: PLAINTIFF:\nL20@P0: DEFENDANT:\nL21@P0: CASE NUMBER:\nL22@P0: APPLICATION AND ORDER TO SERVE SUMMONS BY POSTING\nL23@P0: (Unlawful Detainer)\nL24@P0: Case assigned to:\nL25@P0: Judge:\nL26@P0: Department:\nL27@P0: Date complaint filed:\nL28@P0: Hearing/trial date:\nL29@P0: 1. I am the  plaintiff  plaintiff’s attorney.\nL30@P0: 2. I apply for an order pursuant Section 415.45 of the Code of Civil Procedure to permit service by posting of the\nL31@P0: summons and complaint on defendant(s) (specify names):\nL32@P0: .\nL33@P0: 3. The complaint seeks possession of property located at:\nL34@P0: ,\nL35@P0: County of Orange. The property is  residential  commercial.\nL36@P0: 4. The notice to quit or to pay rent was served by:  personal service  substituted service  posting and mailing\nL37@P0:  other (specify):\nL38@P0: 5. Attempts to serve in a manner specified in Section 415.10 et seq. of the Code of Civil Procedure were made\nL39@P0: (other than posting and publication). The attempts were made as follows:\nL40@P0: DATE TIME REASON SERVICE COULD NOT BE MADE/REMARKS\nL41@P0:  Declaration of process server stating attempts to locate and serve the defendant(s) is attached.\nL42@P0: 6. Service  has  has not been attempted during regular business hours at the place(s) of employment of the\nL43@P0: defendant(s). If not, state reason:  Defendant’s place of employment is unknown.\nL44@P0: Other(specify):\nL45@P0: 7. Did the plaintiff pay for help from a registered unlawful detainer assistant (Bus. And Prof. Code § § 6400-6415)\nL46@P0: Approved for Optional Use\nL47@P0: L690 (Rev. March 2019)\nL48@P0: APPLICATION AND ORDER TO SERVE SUMMONS\nL49@P0: BY POSTING (Unlawful Detainer)\nL50@P0: Page 1 of 2\nL51@P0-1: Civil Code of Procedure, § 415.45who helped prepare this form?  Yes  No. If yes, complete the following information:\nL52@P1: Name of Unlawful Detainer Assistant:\nL53@P1: Address:\nL54@P1: Telephone Number:\nL55@P1: Registration Number:\nL56@P1: County of Registration:\nL57@P1: I declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of California that the foregoing is true and correct.\nL58@P1: Date:\nL59@P1: (TYPE OR PRINT NAME) (SIGNATURE OF APPLICANT OR ATTORNEY)\nL60@P1: FINDINGS AND ORDER\nL61@P1: THE COURT FINDS:\nL62@P1: 1. The defendant(s) named in the application cannot with reasonable diligence be served in any manner\nL63@P1: specified in Section 415.10 et seq. of the Code of Civil Procedure, other than posting or publication.\nL64@P1: 2. (a) A cause of action exists against the defendant(s) named in the application; or (b) the defendant(s)\nL65@P1: named in the application has or claims an interest in real property in California that is subject to the\nL66@P1: jurisdiction of the court; or (c) the relief demanded in the complaint consists wholly or partially in\nL67@P1: excluding the defendant(s) from any interest in the property.\nL68@P1: THE COURT ORDERS:\nL69@P1: The defendant(s) named in the application may be served by posting a copy of the summons and complaint on\nL70@P1: the premises in a manner most likely to give actual notice to the defendant(s), and by immediately mailing, by\nL71@P1: certified mail, a copy of the summons and complaint to the defendant(s) at his or her last known address.\nL72@P1: Date:\nL73@P1: JUDICIAL OFFICER\nL74@P1: Approved for Optional Use\nL75@P1: L690 (Rev. March 2019)\nL76@P1: APPLICATION AND ORDER TO SERVE SUMMONS\nL77@P1: BY POSTING (Unlawful Detainer)\nL78@P1: Page 2 of 2\nL79@P1: Civil Code of Procedure, § 415.45\nL80@P1: For your protection and privacy, please press the Clear This Form\nL81@P1: button after you are done printing this form.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nl1051 (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/l1051.pdf)\nciteturn1031view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1005view3\",\"id\":317}); Total lines: 39\nL0@P0: L-1051\nL1@P0: Approved for Optional Use\nL2@P0: L-1051 (Rev. July 1, 2013)\nL3@P0: APPLICATION FOR WRIT OF POSSESSION\nL4@P0: UNLAWFUL DETAINER\nL5@P0: Code of Civil Procedure,\nL6@P0: §§ 712.010, 715.010, 415.46\nL7@P0: ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name, State Bar number, and address):\nL8@P0: TELEPHONE NO.: FAX NO. (Optional):\nL9@P0: E-MAIL ADDRESS (Optional):\nL10@P0: ATTORNEY FOR (Name):\nL11@P0: FOR COURT USE ONLY\nL12@P0: SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF ORANGE\nL13@P0: JUSTICE CENTER:\nL14@P0: Central – 700 Civic Center Dr. West, Santa Ana, CA 92701-4045\nL15@P0: Harbor – 4601 Jamboree Rd., Newport Beach, CA 92660-2595\nL16@P0: North – 1275 N. Berkeley Ave., P.O. Box 5000, Fullerton, CA 92838-0500\nL17@P0: West – 8141 13th St., Westminster, CA 92683-4593\nL18@P0: PLAINTIFF:\nL19@P0: DEFENDANT:\nL20@P0: CASE NUMBER:\nL21@P0: APPLICATION FOR WRIT OF POSSESSION\nL22@P0: UNLAWFUL DETAINER\nL23@P0: Unlimited civil actions only. Case assigned to:\nL24@P0: Judge:\nL25@P0: Department:\nL26@P0: Date complaint filed:\nL27@P0: Hearing/trial date:\nL28@P0: I am the plaintiff plaintiff's attorney in the above entitled action and hereby apply for a Writ\nL29@P0: of Possession under Sections 712.010 and 715.010 of the Code of Civil Procedure.\nL30@P0: The daily rental value of the property at issue as of the date the complaint for unlawful detainer was\nL31@P0: filed is $ .\nL32@P0: A Prejudgment Claim of Right to Possession has been served in compliance with Section 415.46\nL33@P0: of the Code of Civil Procedure. The writ shall apply to all tenants, subtenants, named claimants, and\nL34@P0: other occupants of the premises.\nL35@P0: I declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of California that the foregoing is true\nL36@P0: and correct.\nL37@P0: Date:\nL38@P0: (TYPE OR PRINT NAME) (SIGNATURE OF PARTY OR ATTORNEY)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nl982.pdf (https://www.occourts.org/s